WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:06.512
Regular expressions are useful when simple literal functions are not enough.

00:00:06.512 --> 00:00:09.612
REGEXP_REPLACE can remove or standardize patterns.

00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:15.632
The tilde operator checks whether a string matches a pattern.

00:00:15.632 --> 00:00:19.852
Regex is powerful, so keep the rule as simple and explainable as possible.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:27.242
A complicated expression that nobody can review is a data-quality risk of its own.

00:00:27.242 --> 00:00:32.377
Connect this idea to a CRM standardizing names, emails, and phone numbers.

00:00:32.377 --> 00:00:38.272
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.272 --> 00:00:44.057
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:44.057 --> 00:00:52.112
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:57.360
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
